# Nunjucks Templates

## Role in Form Journeys

Nunjucks is the template engine that renders all form pages. Templates use GOV.UK Frontend macros and follow strict patterns for paths, conditionals, and error handling.

## Template Path Format (CRITICAL)

**Always use journey name prefix in template paths:**

```javascript
// ✅ Correct
return h.view('journey-name/start', { ... })
return h.view('hello-world/preference', { ... })

// ❌ Wrong - causes 500 errors
return h.view('start', { ... })
return h.view('preference', { ... })
```

Template paths must match: `{journey-name}/{template-name}` where:

- `journey-name` matches directory in `src/server/forms/`
- `template-name` matches `.njk` filename (without extension)

**Critical**: Wrong template paths cause 500 Internal Server Error. See [src/server/forms/hello-world/controller.js](mdc:src/server/forms/hello-world/controller.js) for correct examples.

## Template Structure

### Extending Base Layout

All pages extend the base layout:

```njk
{% extends 'layouts/page.njk' %}
```

### Importing Macros

Import GOV.UK components:

```njk
{% from "govuk/components/input/macro.njk" import govukInput %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/back-link/macro.njk" import govukBackLink %}
```

### Block Structure

```njk
{% block beforeContent %}
  {{ govukBackLink({ href: backLink }) }}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <!-- Page content -->
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
```

## Conditional Syntax

### Use if Expressions (Not Ternary)

❌ **Never use ternary with null:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: error ? { text: error } : null
}) }}
```

✅ **Use if expression:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error
}) }}
```

This syntax works for any conditional property:

- `errorMessage: { text: error } if error`
- `value: email if email`
- `hint: { text: hint } if hint`

### Conditional Rows in Summary Lists

Show rows conditionally:

```njk
{{ govukSummaryList({
  rows: [
    {
      key: { text: "Always shown" },
      value: { text: value }
    },
    {
      key: { text: "Conditional" },
      value: { text: conditionalValue }
    } if condition === "value"
  ]
}) }}
```

### Conditional Blocks

Use if blocks for larger sections:

```njk
{% if error %}
  {{ govukErrorSummary({
    titleText: "There is a problem",
    errorList: [{ text: error, href: "#field" }]
  }) }}
{% endif %}
```

## Variable Access

Access data passed from controller:

```njk
<h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
<p>{{ fieldValue }}</p>
```

Access session data (if passed):

```njk
<p>{{ request.yar.get('field') }}</p>
```

Use filters:

```njk
{{ value | capitalize }}
{{ value | lower }}
```

## Common Mistakes

### Wrong Template Paths (500 Errors)

**Problem**: Using incorrect template paths causes 500 Internal Server Error.

❌ **Wrong:**

```javascript
return h.view('start', { ... })
return h.view('summary', { ... })
```

✅ **Correct:**

```javascript
return h.view('journey-name/start', { ... })
return h.view('journey-name/summary', { ... })
```

**Why it fails**: Hapi can't find template files because they're in `src/server/forms/{journey}/views/` but path doesn't include journey name.

### Using null in Macros (500 Errors)

**Problem**: Using `null` in conditional macro parameters causes template rendering to crash.

❌ **Never:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: error ? { text: error } : null
}) }}
```

✅ **Always:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error
}) }}
```

**Why it fails**: Nunjucks doesn't handle `null` values in macro parameters.

### Ternary Operators Instead of if Expressions

Nunjucks does NOT support JavaScript-style ternary operators (`? :`). Use if expressions or move complex logic to the controller.

❌ **Never use JavaScript ternary:**

```njk
{% set value = condition ? "yes" : "no" %}
href: condition ? ROUTES.PAGE_A : ROUTES.PAGE_B
```

✅ **Use if expressions for simple conditionals:**

```njk
value: { text: error } if error
```

✅ **Move complex logic to controller (RECOMMENDED for complex conditionals):**

```javascript
// Controller
const status = complexCondition ? 'Added' : 'Not added'
const link = application.hasFile ? ROUTES.UPLOAD : ROUTES.MAP
return h.view('page', { status, link })
```

```njk
{{ govukSummaryList({
  rows: [{
    value: { text: status },
    actions: { items: [{ href: link }] }
  }]
}) }}
```

**Pattern**: For complex conditionals involving multiple conditions or ROUTES objects, compute values in the controller and pass simple variables to the template.

### Missing Journey Name Prefix

Template paths without journey name prefix will fail. Always include it.

### Incorrect Block Names

Use correct block names:

- `{% block beforeContent %}` - For back links
- `{% block content %}` - For main page content

## Form Structure in Templates

Forms must use proper structure:

```njk
<form method="post" novalidate>
  {{ govukInput({ name: "field", ... }) }}
  {{ govukButton({ text: "Continue" }) }}
</form>
```

- Always `method="post"` (never GET for submissions)
- Include `novalidate` attribute
- Submit button inside form (not link)

## Passing Data to Templates

Controllers pass data as second argument to `h.view()`:

```javascript
return h.view('journey-name/page', {
  pageTitle: 'Title',
  heading: 'Heading',
  error,
  ROUTES // Pass entire object, not individual routes
})
```

Templates access via variable names: `{{ heading }}`, `{{ ROUTES.PAGE }}`.

## Common Mistakes

### Error Summary href Must Match Actual Field

When displaying error summaries for conditional forms (where different fields are shown based on user selections), the `href` in the error summary must dynamically match the actual field being displayed:

❌ **Hardcoded href that doesn't match conditional field:**

```njk
{% if error %}
  {{ govukErrorSummary({
    errorList: [{
      text: error,
      href: "#hotelCount"  // Wrong if HMO or Residential institution selected
    }]
  }) }}
{% endif %}
```

✅ **Dynamic href based on conditional field:**

```njk
{% if error %}
  {% set errorField = "hotelCount" if "Hotel" in selectedBuildingTypes else ("hmoCount" if "House of multiple occupation (HMO)" in selectedBuildingTypes else "residentialInstitutionCount") %}
  {{ govukErrorSummary({
    errorList: [{
      text: error,
      href: "#" + errorField
    }]
  }) }}
{% endif %}
```

**Pattern**: For conditional forms where different input fields are shown based on user selections, use Nunjucks conditional logic to set the correct field name for the error summary href.

## Known Issues

### Template Rendering Error (500) with Incorrect Template Paths

**Problem**: Using incorrect template paths in `h.view()` calls causes 500 Internal Server Error.

**Root Cause**: Templates are located in `src/server/forms/{journey}/views/` but path doesn't include journey name prefix.

**Solution**: Always use `{journey-name}/{template-name}` format:

```javascript
return h.view('journey-name/start', { ... })
```

**Example**: See [src/server/forms/hello-world/controller.js](mdc:src/server/forms/hello-world/controller.js) line 8 for correct template path:

```javascript
return h.view('forms/hello-world/views/start', { ... })
```

### Template Rendering Error (500) with Conditional Properties

**Problem**: Using ternary operators or `null` in Nunjucks macro parameters causes 500 Internal Server Error.

**Root Cause**: Nunjucks doesn't handle `null` values in macro parameters properly.

**Solution**: Use if expression syntax:

```njk
errorMessage: { text: error } if error
```

**Example**: See [src/server/forms/hello-world/views/name.njk](mdc:src/server/forms/hello-world/views/name.njk) line 41-43 for correct conditional error message pattern.

